        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "The grep -c/set -e abort and the dasel fallback were both found and fixed properly (git diff --cached --quiet; tomllib read that fails loudly), but commit signing was never addressed in the script or workflow, so a runner with a global commit.gpgsign still breaks the commit; the test masks this by pointing GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL at /dev/null, so the cap applies."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 5,
        "rationale": "Build failures still fail the job, real changes are still committed and pushed, and data/ is untouched, but the agent rewrote build-snapshot.sh (tail to awk, LC_ALL=C, which can reorder the existing snapshot and cause a spurious commit), added a concurrency group, and added a 128-line test harness, none of which were asked for."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "The reply clearly explains the non-zero grep exit inside a command substitution under set -e and the missing tool hidden by the || echo unknown fallback, but it never mentions the global signing setting the script cannot see, so a reader would not learn why that path was unsafe."
      }
    ],
